- ### References by key
+ ### Références par clé

- A reference need not come from a store at all. Where an entity carries its own key, such as an
- email address or a product code, a `Reference` to it is that key, typed by what it refers to. A
- `Resolvable` instance says how a key finds its entity. This one is built from a set of values,
- and searches them by the field marked `@primary`:
+ Une référence n'a pas à provenir d'un stockage. Lorsqu'une entité porte sa propre clé, comme une
+ adresse email ou un code produit, une `Reference` vers elle est cette clé, typée par ce à quoi
+ elle fait référence. Une instance de `Resolvable` dit comment une clé trouve son entité. Celle-ci
+ est construite à partir d'un ensemble de valeurs, et les parcourt d'après le champ marqué
+ `@primary` :

= and searches them by the field marked `@primary`:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- case class Person(@primary email: Text, name: Text)
+ case class Person(@primary email: Text, name: Text)

- val romeo = Person(t"romeo@example.com", t"Romeo")
+ val romeo = Person(t"romeo@example.com", t"Romeo")

- val juliet = Person(t"juliet@example.com", t"Juliet")
+ val juliet = Person(t"juliet@example.com", t"Juliet")

- given personResolvable: (Person is Resolvable by Text) = Resolvable(Set(romeo, juliet))
+ given personResolvable: (Person is Resolvable by Text) = Resolvable(Set(romeo, juliet))

= given personResolvable: (Person is Resolvable by Text) = Resolvable(Set(romeo, juliet))
- ```
+ ```

- With that in scope, `ref` takes the reference of a value, which holds nothing but its key.
